**Proof.** The scored output of an allocation is
$\sum_{S,c,r}g^C_{S,c}(r)T^C_{S,c,r}$. For each schedule this is at most
$w_S\sum_cM^C_{S,c}$, so the total is at most $B_C(y)$.
Choose one maximizing schedule and, independently as counterfactual
choices, a maximizing label in every cell. This is one legitimate
complete deterministic table and attains the bound. Summing all cap rows
with the same weights gives $T_0+\sum_it_ia_i-We$, proving (156.2).

Every integer in the support table is obtained from (156.1) and the
sparse weights. For $O$ pairs, equivalently replace the $N$ contributions
at $00,01$ by their sum before taking that cell's maximum. Thus the table
certifies both full supports without a restriction on witness support.
Evaluating $R$ on all words gives the displayed last column. In particular
it is the same maximizer for all 65 scores, rather than separate favorable
schedules selected for separate inequalities. $\square$

